          "evasion": "graph-camouflage",
          "rail_class": "card-auth"
        },
        "why_kept": "Token-requestor fan-out across many merchants plays the graph role without a beneficiary leg (ATK-T2). Excluding it would have removed a real family.\n"
      },
      {
        "cell_pattern": {
          "evasion": "label-attack",
          "locus": "synthetic-identity"
        },
        "why_kept": "WE DREW THIS RULE AND THEN WITHDREW IT, and the withdrawal is recorded because it raised our own denominator (making our coverage percentage worse) rather than lowering it. The rule read: \"a manufactured identity has no dispute standing, so it cannot corrupt a label channel it never touches.\" That is false for two families we ship. ATK-D2 (representment-evidence poisoning) is a fraudulently-onboarded ACCEPTOR -- which our projection maps to the synthetic-identity locus -- and an acceptor has full dispute standing: defending representments is precisely what it does. ATK-Z2 (slow-drip retrain contamination) corrupts the label DISTRIBUTION through volume, needing no complaint channel at all. Both were inexpressible under the rule.\n"
      }
    ],
